# shell: both
# open: /dev/shm
# volume: not-mine
# AW-096/CW-034: Unmount is a real command reached from the keyboard, and
# an unmount that cannot happen says so instead of doing nothing.  Shown a
# VOLUME -- /dev/shm is one on every Linux, where /tmp is one only on
# some -- because a folder that is no volume gets a status line, not a
# refusal, and that is a different row.
wait 8
expect-title shm
note Cmd+U on the volume being shown; without the right to unmount it,
note the refusal is said out loud rather than nothing happening
key u ctrl
wait 15
expect-alert could not be unmounted
key Escape
wait 3
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt
quit
